@startuml chooser_flow
title paddock: the chooser, questions in and one plan out

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

start
:herdr popup runs `paddock`\n(no subcommand means `choose`);

if (subcommand) then (profiles)
  :print one line per profile:\nagent, workdir, network;
  stop
elseif (launch <profile>) then
  :load the saved profile\n(--cwd shares that directory instead);
  :plan = NewSession(profile);
elseif (attach <session>) then
  :plan = Attach(session ref, cwd only if --cwd was given);
else (choose)
  :sessions.list_sessions();
  if (what kind of window?) then (Local)
    :plan = Local(cwd);
  elseif (Attach:\noffered only when a session is live) then
    :pick a session by name, agent,\nprofile and tab count;
    :plan = Attach(session id):\nthe session keeps its own workdir;
  else (New sandbox session)
    partition "permissions questionnaire" {
      repeat
        :ask the next question, in order:\nstart from a saved profile or Custom;\nagent from the registry, or a command typed in;\ntools: candidates on PATH plus the profile's own,\nmarked when missing; network presets and typed\ndomains; skills under the agent's config dir\n(none, or a different agent: skipped);\nshare a host directory?; session name;\nsave the answers as a profile?;
      repeat while (← Back on a list question?) is (yes: the question before it,\nevery answer so far kept) not (no)
    }
    partition "summary" {
      repeat
        :one line per answer: start from, agent,\ntyped command, tools, network presets and\ndomains, skills, shared dir, name, save as;
      repeat while (Launch, Edit a step, or Cancel?) is (Edit a step: ask\nthat one question again) not (Launch)
    }
    :plan = NewSession(profile, name, save as);
  endif
endif

if (--dry-run) then (yes)
  :print what would happen;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:save the profile and remember a typed-in\nagent, if the answers asked for it;
:sessions.launch_local\n| get_session then attach\n| launch;
:print the pane id;
stop

note right
  Ctrl-C or escape answers None at any question,
  and Cancel on the summary says the same thing:
  the chooser returns no plan and cli.py stops.
  Only cli.py acts on a plan; the chooser reads
  the session list and nothing else. So backing
  out cannot leave a pane or a file behind.

  Back on the first question of the questionnaire
  goes back to "what kind of window?". Text boxes
  carry no Back entry; the summary edits those.
  Editing the agent asks for its skills again,
  because they come from its own config dir.
end note

@enduml
